  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Multi-Currency Implementation Specification</h2>
<p>The application features a strict, production-tested multi-currency architecture designed to support global expenses without cross-rate conversion errors:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Isolated Ledger Accounting:</strong> Expenses retain their native currency (<code>INR</code>, <code>USD</code>, <code>EUR</code>, <code>GBP</code>, <code>AED</code>). Amounts are stored in minor currency units (paise/cents) to eliminate floating-point precision loss.</li>
  <li><strong>Separated Summary Calculations:</strong> When multiple currencies exist within the same billing period, dashboard hero cards and expense summaries render dedicated total chips for each currency rather than summing incompatible figures.</li>
  <li><strong>Reactive State Propagation:</strong> <code>currencyProvider</code> coordinates global defaults while <code>DailyExpenseItemModel</code> tracks item-level currency metadata.</li>
  <li><strong>CSV / XLSX Export:</strong> Exported financial sheets provide dedicated currency columns and per-currency summary totals.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Layer Breakdown & Implementation Patterns</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Feature-First Architecture:</strong> Codebase structured under <code>lib/features/{feature}/{data,domain,presentation}</code> ensuring high cohesion and loose coupling.</li>
  <li><strong>Reactive State (Riverpod):</strong> <code>AsyncValue&lt;T&gt;</code> encapsulates <code>loading</code>, <code>data</code>, and <code>error</code> states with automatic dependency invalidation on CRUD mutations.</li>
  <li><strong>Hardware Secure Storage:</strong> AES-256 Android Keystore and iOS Keychain encrypt all JWT tokens at rest, eliminating token leakage.</li>
  <li><strong>Zero-Crash Offline Guard:</strong> Dual DNS socket ping (<code>InternetAddress.lookup</code>) to Google and Cloudflare DNS without buggy native platform channels.</li>
  <li><strong>60s Dio Network Engine:</strong> Queued retry interceptors safeguard against cloud server cold-starts with automatic Bearer token injection.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. REST API Contracts & Endpoint Specifications</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 12%;">Method</th>
      <th style="width: 32%;">Endpoint</th>
      <th>Function & Payload Summary</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/mobile/auth/google</code></td><td>Exchanges Google ID Token for JWT bearer access token & user profile.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/api/mobile/auth/me</code></td><td>Validates existing session and fetches latest user profile data.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/dailyexpense</code></td><td>Fetches monthly expense records, category aggregations, and per-currency totals.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/dailyexpense</code></td><td>Creates a new expense with title, amount, unit price, date, category ID, and currency code.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PUT</td><td><code>/dailyexpense/{id}</code></td><td>Updates an existing expense record with modified fields.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DELETE</td><td><code>/dailyexpense/{id}</code></td><td>Permanently removes the specified expense item from the user's ledger.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/expensetype</code></td><td>Retrieves available expense categories with assigned metadata, icons, and colors.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/chart-data</code></td><td>Provides multi-series time-series and categorical aggregates for analytics charts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/ai/chat</code></td><td>Streams conversational messages to the AI engine with conversational memory.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/api/ai/confirm-classification</code></td><td>Applies AI-detected expense proposal directly into the user's expense ledger.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>7. Central API & Endpoints Configuration</h2>
<p>All backend server configurations and endpoint URLs can be modified in a single location:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Master Configuration:</strong> <code>lib/core/config/app_config.dart</code></li>
  <li><strong>Endpoints URI Registry:</strong> <code>lib/core/networking/api_endpoints.dart</code></li>
  <li><strong>Base URL & Environment:</strong> <code>.env</code> and <code>lib/core/constants/app_constants.dart</code></li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Build, Signing & Deployment Verification</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Target SDKs:</strong> Android <code>minSdk: 23</code>, <code>targetSdk: 35</code>, <code>compileSdk: 36</code> | iOS <code>14.0+</code></li>
  <li><strong>Build Commands:</strong><br/>
    <code>flutter build appbundle --release</code> (Android Google Play Release)<br/>
    <code>flutter build ipa --release</code> (Apple App Store Release)
  </li>
  <li><strong>Release Quality:</strong> Certified 0 lint issues, 0 crash vulnerabilities, clean analyzer output.</li>
</ul>

